    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Mickey Moniak** leads the way as our highest-scoring option with a 74.96 efficiency rating. He benefits from a premier setup against Gray, where a combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) elevates his output, making him a must-start in the two-hole. **Corbin Carroll** follows closely behind at 71.26; despite a slightly tougher matchup against Leahy, his elite speed profile and the stability of hitting third against a right-handed arm keep him in the upper echelon of our daily projections. **Josh Naylor** rounds out our top trio (68.78), as he squares off against Keller, where a significant SP skill edge (+11%) provides a massive boost to his base projection.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Zach McKinstry**, who sat on the bubble with a 52.58 score. While he enjoyed a solid park factor and a favorable platoon look against Rod\u00f3n, he was ultimately edged out by **Travis Bazzana** and **Max Muncy** due to their more advantageous lineup spots and current efficiency trends. We are also keeping a watchful eye on **James Wood**; his 53.36 score is depressed by a difficult matchup against Luzardo\u2019s elite holding ability, though his 0.404 xwOBA keeps him active. Owners should note that **Austin Riley** carries a slight risk despite his start; while he faces a left-hander, we are monitoring his slow SP delivery against the runner, which could provide opportunistic stolen base chances if he reaches, but his low spot in the order slightly caps his overall upside. \n\nFinally, as we manage our game caps, we continue to keep **Jose Caballero** and **Cole Young** on the bench. **Jose Caballero** represents a high-risk, high-reward profile, but his low efficiency today\u2014driven by a poor platoon matchup\u2014precluded him from the starting nine. With **Trevor Story** remaining on the IL and players like **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Carson Williams**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Henry Bolte** waiting in the wings, we are maintaining a disciplined approach to our daily efficiency targets to ensure we don't bleed innings unnecessarily.",
